@startuml sequence-US6
' File: sequence-US6.wsd
' Description: Sequence diagram for US6 (Submit code and get graded),
'     showing how a submission moves through the presentation, business
'     logic, and data access layers and the sandbox runner container.
' Author(s): <team member names>

title US6: Submit code and get graded

actor Player
participant "game.js\n(browser)" as JS
participant "GameRoutes\n(presentation)" as Routes
participant "GameService\n(business)" as Game
participant "GradingService\n(business)" as Grading
participant "RunnerClient\n(business)" as RunnerClient
participant "Runner\n(container)" as Runner
participant "ScoreCalculator\n(business)" as Score
participant "DialogueService\n(business)" as Dialogue
participant "GameRun\n(model)" as Run
participant "RunRepository\n(data)" as Repo
database "PostgreSQL\n(container)" as DB

Player -> JS : click Submit
JS -> Routes : POST /runs/{run_id}/submit {code}
Routes -> Game : submit_stage(user, run_id, code)

Game -> Repo : get_active_run(run_id, user)
Repo -> DB : SELECT run, stage, check script
DB --> Repo : rows
Repo --> Game : GameRun, Stage

Game -> Grading : grade(code, stage.check_script)
Grading -> RunnerClient : grade(code, check_script, limits)
RunnerClient -> Runner : POST /grade
loop each turn, stopping at the first broken rule, crash, or timeout
    Runner -> Runner : program prints a screen\n(until it asks for input or exits)
    Runner -> Runner : check script reads the screen\nand checks the stage's rules
    opt the stage reads input
        Runner -> Runner : check script types one input line
    end
end
note right of Runner : The check script never reads\nthe player's code. No LLM call.
Runner --> RunnerClient : verdict, reason, rule, turn, inputs, last screen, traceback
RunnerClient --> Grading : RunnerResult
Grading --> Game : Verdict

alt verdict passed
    Game -> Score : stage_points(seconds_remaining, difficulty)
    Score --> Game : points
    Game -> Run : advance_stage(code, points)
else verdict failed
    Game -> Run : lose_life()
end

Game -> Repo : save(run, submission)
Repo -> DB : INSERT submission, INSERT checkpoint on a pass, UPDATE run
DB --> Repo : ok

Game -> Dialogue : line_for(event)
Dialogue --> Game : Overlord line

Game --> Routes : SubmitResult
Routes --> JS : 200 OK (JSON)
JS --> Player : verdict, lives, Overlord line, next stage

@enduml
